132
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:47,082
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why you would not... you would also want to not be touched by that pain in the first place.

133
00:11:49,330 --> 00:11:55,915
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you tame your senses, the desires will fade, the pressures will lessen, and you'll be factually more content and happier.

134
00:12:00,178 --> 00:12:04,161
[SPEAKER_03]: So, you need like, I don't know, 80% physical seclusion, not 100%.

135
00:12:04,181 --> 00:12:05,882
[SPEAKER_03]: There's no point in it.

136
00:12:08,803 --> 00:12:13,547
[SPEAKER_03]: And so, just so that you have a basis for seeing your mind, having things calm down.

137
00:12:14,668 --> 00:12:26,138
[SPEAKER_03]: So, like this, like this monastery is a probably like an 80% physical seclusion place, so that you can actually do the... try get into the real solitude.

138
00:12:26,418 --> 00:12:26,678
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah.

139
00:12:26,758 --> 00:12:28,880
[SPEAKER_03]: Of 100% mental seclusion.

140
00:12:29,237 --> 00:12:29,777
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, that's the thing.

141
00:12:29,797 --> 00:12:31,738
[SPEAKER_01]: The real solitude will be that mental.

142
00:12:31,958 --> 00:12:32,998
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, that's what you said.

143
00:12:33,018 --> 00:12:35,419
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there is not like 100% physical solitude.

144
00:12:35,919 --> 00:12:39,000
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, you can aim for it, but that means you're overshooting the mark now.

145
00:12:39,620 --> 00:12:39,780
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

146
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:42,561
[SPEAKER_01]: You know, there are empty rooms, empty huts, empty roots of a tree.

147
00:12:43,241 --> 00:12:46,442
[SPEAKER_01]: Go there, monks, and contemplate things, basically.

148
00:12:46,542 --> 00:12:58,085
[SPEAKER_01]: So, as I said, there is a... somebody who starts that way can become too precious, but it won't be hard to see, if you're honest, that that preciousness comes from, oh, I don't want to be bothered.

149
00:12:59,122 --> 00:13:00,063
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, I resist it.

150
00:13:00,344 --> 00:13:04,890
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm averse to the idea of... so that's why I'm secluded.

151
00:13:05,450 --> 00:13:07,513
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, well, no, then I should be bothered.

152
00:13:08,654 --> 00:13:14,182
[SPEAKER_01]: Not by something terribly unwholesome, but by duties, or answering a question, and so on.

153
00:13:15,463 --> 00:13:16,805
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, well, if that bothers me,

154
